        name of the scan-data input pin/port of the chain 
    [-hookup_pin_sdi <pin|hpin>]:
        core side hookup pin for SDI 
    [-sdo <string>]:
        name of the scan-data output pin/port of the chain 
    [-hookup_pin_sdo <pin|hpin>]:
        core side hookup pin for SDO 
    [-analyze]:
        analyze an existing scan chain 
    [-create_ports]:
        create SDI/SDO ports if they do not exist 
    [-shared_output]:
        whether the scan-data output pin/port is shared with a functional connection 
    [-shared_input]:
        whether the scan-data input pin/port is shared with a functional connection 
    [-non_shared_output]:
        whether the scan-data output pin/port is not shared with a functional connection 
    [-shared_select <test_signal>]:
        name of the test signal for the shared out mux 
    [-shift_enable <test_signal>]:
        name of the shift-enable signal for chain 
    [-head <scan_segment>]:
        name of user-defined segment to be placed at the head of chain 
    [-tail <scan_segment>]:
        name of user-defined segment to be placed at the tail of chain 
    [-body <scan_segment>]:
        name of user-defined segment to be placed in the middle (if head and tail specified) or anywhere in chain 
    [-complete]:
        indicates the included segments define a complete chain 
    [-domain <test_clock_domain>]:
        name of test-clock domain (see 'define_dft test_clock' command) 
    [-edge <string>]:
        use only flip-flops active on this edge {rise|fall} 
    [-max_length <integer>]:
        length of chain (when '-complete' option is not used) 
    [-cfg_pad <test_signal>]:
        configure connected pads using the test-signal 
    [-terminal_lockup <string>]:
        type of lockup element inserted at the tail end of chain ('level_sensitive' or 'edge_sensitive') 
    [-dont_overlay]:
        do not overlay the user defined segments onto the actual scan chain when specified with the -analyzed option 
